=================================================================
  SYNTHESIS: THE BLUE LINE SKELETON
=================================================================

  The BLUE LINE (SC tournaments) occupies a special position:
  1. SC spans the FULL H range (both min and max)
  2. NSC is CONSTRAINED to a NARROW H range
  3. At equal H, SC has MORE linear paths (higher L)
     and FEWER Hamiltonian cycles (lower HC)
  4. Breaking symmetry (leaving the blue line) converts
     linear paths into cyclic paths: L -> HC
  5. The ARBORESCENCE count distinguishes SC from NSC
     even within the same score class

  THE SKELETON IS THE TRADE-OFF CURVE:
  SC lives on the L-rich, HC-poor side (tree-like)
  NSC lives on the L-poor, HC-rich side (cycle-like)
  H = n*HC + L is the BUDGET CONSTRAINT
  Symmetry-breaking REALLOCATES the budget from L to HC
